+
+## UBU-D0347: Relationship transition Steps bind user actions and scoped refusal closure
+
+**Status:** Accepted → DESIGN.md §22.3.3. Resolves `UBU-Q0097`; refines `UBU-D0155` within `UBU-D0345` and `UBU-D0346`, preserving §22.4's advisory boundary.
+
+Validate every instantiated Step and Task, including nested branches and replacements, with versioned action, completion-test, evidence, applicability/closure and review bindings. Counterparty feelings, assent, decisions, Identity changes, receipt, understanding and performance cannot be user completion requirements or asserted guaranteed effects. Response evidence may govern eligibility, while every branch has finite outcome-independent closure.
+
+Represent `counterparty_autonomy_acknowledgment` as an explicitly user-confirmed, version-bound record of autonomous response, valid decline, no user failure, refusal closure, bounded clarification and new-attempt reopening. It provides neither counterparty consent nor action authority. Deterministic schema/link/version checks remain ordinary admission requirements; semantic behavioral findings retain uncertainty and advisory/user-required review. Bypass cannot establish process success or conformance.
+
+Authentic refusal is a reviewed, sufficiently attributed scoped expression declining or stopping pursuit, including polite, partial and current-attempt refusals. User reports may suffice; no proof of inner sincerity, reason, repetition or recording is required. Silence and uncertainty cannot be converted into refusal or assent. Admit exploratory terminal closure and pursuit-Task retirement using `UBU-D0346`, preserving history and unrelated work without waiting for reflection or emotional recovery.
+
+Permit one proposal and at most one clarification of an ambiguous response to the same proposal, with no reconsideration or persuasion retry. Communication accounting spans Tasks, revisions, channels and Devices. Unknown delivery cannot justify possible duplicate solicitation; transport replay requires established non-delivery or demonstrated idempotent delivery.
+
+Reopening requires a new transition/Objective with lineage, a versioned materially new evidence comparison, current contact boundaries and fresh stronger review. Cooling, user desire and reinterpretation alone are insufficient; changed circumstances grant no consent. DESIGN.md §22.3.3 defines conformance fixtures. This resolves the Phase 2 data-model contract, not implementation acceptance; taxonomy/firewall, pacing/support, review UX and typed evidence policy remain in their existing questions. Phase 1 maintenance is unchanged.
+
